ning attack on\"},\"supplyQueue(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Stores the order of markets on which liquidity is supplied upon deposit.Can contain any market. A market is skipped as soon as its supply cap is reached.\"},\"withdrawQueue(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Stores the order of markets from which liquidity is withdrawn upon withdrawal.Always contain all non-zero cap markets as well as all markets on which the vault supplies liquidity,\"},\"lostAssets()\":{\"details\":\"In order to cover those lost assets, it is advised to supply on behalf of address(1) on the vault\"},\"submitTimelock(uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Reverts if a timelock is already pending. Revoke the pending timelock to overwrite it.In case the new timelock is higher than the current one, the timelock is set immediately.\"},\"revokePendingTimelock()\":{\"details\":\"Does not revert if there is no pending timelock.\"},\"submitCap((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256)\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Reverts if a cap is already pending. Revoke the pending cap to overwrite it.Warning: Reverts if a market removal is pending.In case the new cap is lower than the current one, the cap is set immediately.\"},\"revokePendingCap(bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"Does not revert if there is no pending cap.\"},\"submitMarketRemoval((address,address,address,address,uint256))\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Reverts for non-zero cap or if there is a pending cap. Successfully submitting a zero cap will\"},\"revokePendingMarketRemoval(bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"Does not revert if there is no pending market removal.\"},\"submitGuardian(address)\":{\"details\":\"In case there is no guardian, the gardian is set immediately.Warning: Submitting a gardian will overwrite the current pending gardian.\"},\"setSupplyQueue(bytes32[])\":{\"params\":{\"newSupplyQueue\":\"is an array of enabled markets, and can contain duplicate markets, but it would only\"}},\"updateWithdrawQueue(uint256[])\":{\"details\":\"Warning: Removing a market with supply will decrease the fee accrued until one of the functions updatingWarning: `updateWithdrawQueue` is not idempotent. Submitting twice the same tx will change the queue twice.\",\"params\":{\"indexes\":\"The indexes of each market in the previous withdraw queue, in the new withdraw queue's order.\"}},\"reallocate(((address,address,address,address,uint256),uint256)[])\":{\"details\":\"The behavior of the reallocation can be altered by state changes, including:Sender is expected to pass `assets = type(uint256).max` with the last MarketAllocation of `allocations` toA supply in a reallocation step will make the reallocation revert if the amount is greater than the net\"}},\"details\":\"This interface is inherited by MetaMorphoV1_1 so that function signatures are checked by the compiler.Consider using the IMetaMorphoV1_1 interface instead of this one.\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"config(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the current configuration of each market.\"},\"pendingGuardian()\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the pending guardian.\"},\"pendingCap(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the pending cap for each market.\"},\"pendingTimelock()\":{\"notice\":\"Returns the pending timelock.\"},\"MORPHO()\":{\"notice\":\"The address of the Morpho contract.\"},\"DECIMALS_OFFSET()\":{\"notice\":\"OpenZeppelin decimals offset used by the ERC4626 implementation. empty vault is low (see https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/5.x/erc4626#inflation-attack). To protect against this attack, vault deployers should make an initial deposit of a non-trivial amount in the vault or depositors should check that the share price does not exceed a certain limit.\"},\"curator()\":{\"notice\":\"The address of the curator.\"},\"isAllocator(address)\":{\"notice\":\"Stores whether an address is an allocator or not.\"},\"guardian()\":{\"notice\":\"The current guardian. Can be set even without the timelock set.\"},\"fee()\":{\"notice\":\"The current fee.\"},\"feeRecipie